Z||000008||Formula88||04-11-2001||09:20 AM||||Well, when I go into the local Pep Boys to buy parts, the part guy always laughs or makes some smarta$$ remark when I tell him I have a Fiero.  Next time, I think I'll tell him off and take my business elsewhere.  I'm not overly sensitive, but he expects me to give him my money after he trashes my car?  I don't think so.  I should have said something last time, but was taken off guard and let it go.||||reg||1
Z||000009||LZeitgeist||04-11-2001||12:08 PM||||Be sure to get the manager involved so that they know that *you're* not the one being the a$$hole in the situation... be sweet if you can get the guy fired.<P>Too many retail places just blow off a pi$$ed off customer as someone who was just being an a$$... if the manager relizes that his sale guy is the one with the attitude problem and that he's costing them revenue, I doubt he'll be there much longer.<P>If it *is* the manager giving you sh*t, then call the regional office...||||reg||1
Z||000010||Old Lar||04-11-2001||12:30 PM||||To answer the question "Some people are just dumb!"  the answer is yes, but not about Fieros only.  I was paying for an item at a store with cash and gave the clerk a clad Kennedy half dollar coin as part of the payment, and got this blank stare and question "What kind of coin is this?"  What would happen if I gave her an Eisenhower dollar coin?<P>I love to challenge today's youth intellect.||||reg||9
